{"line_num": "1", "sentence": "Got my APOE results back and I am E3/E4.", "uuid": "c553c275-da04-4c03-bd2c-7868f309a2a0"}
{"line_num": "2", "sentence": "Waiting for my next appt with the NP to discuss next steps.", "uuid": "c553c275-da04-4c03-bd2c-7868f309a2a0"}
{"line_num": "3", "sentence": "I know that E4/E4 is pretty much a no go for Donanemab.", "uuid": "c553c275-da04-4c03-bd2c-7868f309a2a0"}
{"line_num": "4", "sentence": "E3/E4 is supposedly 50% less chance of ARIA, but still a risk.", "uuid": "c553c275-da04-4c03-bd2c-7868f309a2a0"}
{"line_num": "5", "sentence": "My Centiloid is 144.", "uuid": "c553c275-da04-4c03-bd2c-7868f309a2a0"}
{"line_num": "6", "sentence": "So, lots of existing plaques.", "uuid": "c553c275-da04-4c03-bd2c-7868f309a2a0"}
{"line_num": "7", "sentence": "Donanemab is for clearing those.", "uuid": "c553c275-da04-4c03-bd2c-7868f309a2a0"}
{"line_num": "8", "sentence": "Lecanemab is for stoping the formation of new ones.", "uuid": "c553c275-da04-4c03-bd2c-7868f309a2a0"}
{"line_num": "9", "sentence": "I am going to go with what the Doc says.", "uuid": "c553c275-da04-4c03-bd2c-7868f309a2a0"}
{"line_num": "10", "sentence": "But, curious if any of you with a high plaque burden that have started treatment had that discussion with your Doc, and which you eventually got on.", "uuid": "c553c275-da04-4c03-bd2c-7868f309a2a0"}
{"line_num": "11", "sentence": "Thank you.", "uuid": "c553c275-da04-4c03-bd2c-7868f309a2a0"}
{"line_num": "12", "sentence": "I\u2019m in the stage in which I recognize my own diminished cognitive skills, but don\u2019t have a diagnosis yet.", "uuid": "368f05ec-403d-4b14-ac5c-bea6b43f9ba3"}
{"line_num": "13", "sentence": "My job performance is suffering, which is very stressful.", "uuid": "368f05ec-403d-4b14-ac5c-bea6b43f9ba3"}
{"line_num": "14", "sentence": "How did you navigate this phase? Which came first, your diagnosis or problems at work? Did you resign, or use long term disability? Our family relies on my employment for health insurance as well as our primary income.", "uuid": "368f05ec-403d-4b14-ac5c-bea6b43f9ba3"}
{"line_num": "15", "sentence": "Thanks.", "uuid": "368f05ec-403d-4b14-ac5c-bea6b43f9ba3"}
{"line_num": "16", "sentence": "My husband just diagnosed with AD.", "uuid": "c5662d19-a37d-4b1e-80bb-0c254345f4f8"}
{"line_num": "17", "sentence": "His bloodwork \u201ctwo copies of APOE4 allele were detected \u201c.", "uuid": "c5662d19-a37d-4b1e-80bb-0c254345f4f8"}
{"line_num": "18", "sentence": "He also is on Eliquis blood thinner for A fib episode in March 2025.", "uuid": "c5662d19-a37d-4b1e-80bb-0c254345f4f8"}
{"line_num": "19", "sentence": "No recent Afib.", "uuid": "c5662d19-a37d-4b1e-80bb-0c254345f4f8"}
{"line_num": "20", "sentence": "We have upcoming neurology appointment and I have put my hopes on Lequimbi.", "uuid": "c5662d19-a37d-4b1e-80bb-0c254345f4f8"}
{"line_num": "21", "sentence": "After doing research it seems he may not be a good candidate.", "uuid": "c5662d19-a37d-4b1e-80bb-0c254345f4f8"}
{"line_num": "22", "sentence": "Then read about the Watchman that lets a patient come off blood thinners.", "uuid": "c5662d19-a37d-4b1e-80bb-0c254345f4f8"}
{"line_num": "23", "sentence": "Any experience with this anyone? Trying to stay positive grateful and in the moment.", "uuid": "c5662d19-a37d-4b1e-80bb-0c254345f4f8"}
{"line_num": "24", "sentence": "Thank you for any insight Also EOAD sounds scary for rapid progression", "uuid": "c5662d19-a37d-4b1e-80bb-0c254345f4f8"}
{"line_num": "25", "sentence": "I was diagnosed with EO AD last week.", "uuid": "6d689085-3a12-4c56-8fab-0fa31e826505"}
{"line_num": "26", "sentence": "Would love to connect with others in the area.", "uuid": "6d689085-3a12-4c56-8fab-0fa31e826505"}
{"line_num": "27", "sentence": "Maybe meet for coffee or walk.", "uuid": "6d689085-3a12-4c56-8fab-0fa31e826505"}
{"line_num": "28", "sentence": "My wife is 56 years old, she was diagnosed with Early On Set 2 years ago.", "uuid": "adca9829-193a-4781-b0da-d156734f4e6a"}
{"line_num": "29", "sentence": "She has progressed into early stages of moderate.", "uuid": "adca9829-193a-4781-b0da-d156734f4e6a"}
{"line_num": "30", "sentence": "The day she was diagnosed we were given basic slow down med and off we went.", "uuid": "adca9829-193a-4781-b0da-d156734f4e6a"}
{"line_num": "31", "sentence": "They said there were clinical trials we could try etc, but when I look it doesn\u2019t seem to fit her age range etc.", "uuid": "adca9829-193a-4781-b0da-d156734f4e6a"}
{"line_num": "32", "sentence": "I feel like we were sent off like, \u201cGood luck with that.\u201d Although the doctor was great I wasn\u2019t given anything I was supposed to or search for.", "uuid": "adca9829-193a-4781-b0da-d156734f4e6a"}
{"line_num": "33", "sentence": "My wife is FIT, she can\u2019t follow a class any longer but she has personal trainer, yoga etc, lots of walking.", "uuid": "adca9829-193a-4781-b0da-d156734f4e6a"}
{"line_num": "34", "sentence": "She\u2019s able to a lot physically, not near what she once was, but she\u2019s spinning mentally, memory and processing wise.", "uuid": "adca9829-193a-4781-b0da-d156734f4e6a"}
{"line_num": "35", "sentence": "I just feel like I have missed the bus on something out there that could help her.", "uuid": "adca9829-193a-4781-b0da-d156734f4e6a"}
{"line_num": "36", "sentence": "We weren\u2019t really even told how often we should get checked on by the Neuro, so I made an appt (which was 4 months from the day I tried).", "uuid": "adca9829-193a-4781-b0da-d156734f4e6a"}
{"line_num": "37", "sentence": "What am I missing? Also looking for a support group for people her age, (no offense).", "uuid": "adca9829-193a-4781-b0da-d156734f4e6a"}
{"line_num": "38", "sentence": "When I tell people she has ALZ, they can\u2019t seem to grasp that, as in their mind you have to be 75 or older.", "uuid": "adca9829-193a-4781-b0da-d156734f4e6a"}
{"line_num": "39", "sentence": "I'm recently diagnosed positive for early stage Alzheimer.", "uuid": "0ea5fe2d-0328-42a4-948b-5078c124e34a"}
{"line_num": "40", "sentence": "Currently I am taking a prescription to help with some memory issues.", "uuid": "0ea5fe2d-0328-42a4-948b-5078c124e34a"}
{"line_num": "41", "sentence": "My Neurologist wants me to decide on one of two intravenous medicine.", "uuid": "0ea5fe2d-0328-42a4-948b-5078c124e34a"}
{"line_num": "42", "sentence": "I am not crazy about the possible side affects.", "uuid": "0ea5fe2d-0328-42a4-948b-5078c124e34a"}
{"line_num": "43", "sentence": "I would like to hear from someone who is on this one and of any side affects.", "uuid": "0ea5fe2d-0328-42a4-948b-5078c124e34a"}
{"line_num": "44", "sentence": "I am a 60 yo newly diagnosed with Alzheimer's.", "uuid": "b3b621d1-5e2e-4c0a-91e1-fe5742e05c02"}
{"line_num": "45", "sentence": "I am a retired Family Physician who noticed issues approximately 18 months ago and was diagnosed with MCI.", "uuid": "b3b621d1-5e2e-4c0a-91e1-fe5742e05c02"}
{"line_num": "46", "sentence": "I stopped practicing medicine and was given disability benefits.", "uuid": "b3b621d1-5e2e-4c0a-91e1-fe5742e05c02"}
{"line_num": "47", "sentence": "I am fortunate to have had that option but despite all my expertise the process of getting a definitive diagnosis was to say the least frustrating.", "uuid": "b3b621d1-5e2e-4c0a-91e1-fe5742e05c02"}
{"line_num": "48", "sentence": "Particularly as my insurance company kept delaying tests or denying them.", "uuid": "b3b621d1-5e2e-4c0a-91e1-fe5742e05c02"}
{"line_num": "49", "sentence": "Ultimately a spinal tap was done that was non diagnostic but \"suspicious\" per my local neurologist.", "uuid": "b3b621d1-5e2e-4c0a-91e1-fe5742e05c02"}
{"line_num": "50", "sentence": "He requested a PET scan and it was denied by insurance.", "uuid": "b3b621d1-5e2e-4c0a-91e1-fe5742e05c02"}
{"line_num": "51", "sentence": "I am fortunate being in the field and had access to the director of the Alzheimer's department at The University of Pennsylvania.", "uuid": "b3b621d1-5e2e-4c0a-91e1-fe5742e05c02"}
{"line_num": "52", "sentence": "I knew the spinal tap most likely was the answer but I needed to see someone to give me a final answer.", "uuid": "b3b621d1-5e2e-4c0a-91e1-fe5742e05c02"}
{"line_num": "53", "sentence": "After a 3 hour visit at U of P he came into the room and told my wife, brother and I that indeed I had Alzheimer's.", "uuid": "b3b621d1-5e2e-4c0a-91e1-fe5742e05c02"}
{"line_num": "54", "sentence": "I am currently undergoing Lequembi and plan on doing my best to be productive as long as possible.", "uuid": "b3b621d1-5e2e-4c0a-91e1-fe5742e05c02"}
{"line_num": "55", "sentence": "I have decided to share my journey as a physician with Alzheimer's through social media.", "uuid": "b3b621d1-5e2e-4c0a-91e1-fe5742e05c02"}
{"line_num": "56", "sentence": "I know what the ultimate outcome will be but I have always been someone who has called it like it is so I want to share how I will deal with this and hope to help others while trying to help myself.", "uuid": "b3b621d1-5e2e-4c0a-91e1-fe5742e05c02"}
{"line_num": "57", "sentence": "This is just the beginning of my Alzheimer's journey and hope to be able to share more here as time goes on.", "uuid": "b3b621d1-5e2e-4c0a-91e1-fe5742e05c02"}
{"line_num": "58", "sentence": "I was recently diagnosed in early December and have been more worried about how my partner is going to handle being a caregiver\u2026.", "uuid": "0c3a8b99-a077-4873-b031-c46f2507b3fc"}
{"line_num": "59", "sentence": "He is a very sensitive thoughtful and caring person but also suffers from depression.", "uuid": "0c3a8b99-a077-4873-b031-c46f2507b3fc"}
{"line_num": "60", "sentence": "Hence my concern\u2026.he did go to one caregiver support meeting.", "uuid": "0c3a8b99-a077-4873-b031-c46f2507b3fc"}
{"line_num": "61", "sentence": "I'm 58 years old and have been diagnosed with early onset Alzheimer's.", "uuid": "a11e89fc-190b-4cd3-945a-481aa5a26adb"}
{"line_num": "62", "sentence": "I would like to talk with those who have early onset also.", "uuid": "a11e89fc-190b-4cd3-945a-481aa5a26adb"}
{"line_num": "63", "sentence": "I'm hoping that others who have had brain swelling as a side effect of Kisunla can give me some ideas and some hope.", "uuid": "a195f1be-6404-42ee-8832-72214a304a2f"}
{"line_num": "64", "sentence": "I've had a really easy time with Kisunla (Donanemab) since I started in August, and all of my MRIs were perfect.", "uuid": "a195f1be-6404-42ee-8832-72214a304a2f"}
{"line_num": "65", "sentence": "There was break in MRIs from month 5 to month 7, but when I had my MRI last week in preparation for the 7th infusion they found brain swelling in the occipital cortex (I have PCA - the type of early Alzheimer's that starts with neuro-visuel symptoms, so in the occipital cortex).", "uuid": "a195f1be-6404-42ee-8832-72214a304a2f"}
{"line_num": "66", "sentence": "So, they didn't give me that 7th infusion of Kisunla, and instead gave me 3 days of heavy steroids by infusion (plus 9 days of steroids to take at home).", "uuid": "a195f1be-6404-42ee-8832-72214a304a2f"}
{"line_num": "67", "sentence": "Once they identified it on the MRI I realized that I probably should have known, because I've been dizzy and nauseated, and I've also had really weird spasms in my hands and feet and stomach.", "uuid": "a195f1be-6404-42ee-8832-72214a304a2f"}
{"line_num": "68", "sentence": "Now I'm really freaked out that this brain swelling won't go down, and that I won't be allowed to continue the Kisunla (which has been making a difference).", "uuid": "a195f1be-6404-42ee-8832-72214a304a2f"}
{"line_num": "69", "sentence": "I'm still dizzy and light-headed and feeling icky, like I have the flu.", "uuid": "a195f1be-6404-42ee-8832-72214a304a2f"}
{"line_num": "70", "sentence": "Any ideas about how to reduce the brain swelling? Any thoughts from people who have lived through this, and then gotten back on the Kisunla??", "uuid": "a195f1be-6404-42ee-8832-72214a304a2f"}
{"line_num": "71", "sentence": "Common Abbreviations People ADLO = Loved One with Alzheimer's disease BF = Boyfriend BIL = Brother-in-Law DD = Dear/Darling Daughter DH = Dear Husband DS = Dear/Darling Son DW = Dear/Darling Wife FIL = Father-in-Law GF = Girlfriend GLO = Greetings to Loved Ones GMIL = Grandmother-in-Law GFIL = Grandfather-in-Law LO = Loved One MIL = Mother-in-Law NOK = Next of Kin OH = Other Half PWD/PLWD = Person with Dementia/Person Living with dementia\\ SIBs = Brothers and Sisters or Siblings SIL = Sister-in-Law SO = Significant Other Popular Online Acronyms AKA = Also known as BBL = Be back later BTW = By the way BRB = Be right back IMCO = In my considered opinion IMHO = In my humble/honest opinion IOW = In other words J/K = Just kidding LOL = Laugh out loud OMG = Oh my gosh! OT = Off topic TIA = Thanks in advance TTT = \u201cto the top\u201d TTYL = Talk to you later WDYT = What do you think Types of Dementia AD or ALZ = Alzheimer's disease ADRD = Alzheimer's disease and related dementias EO or EOAD = Early onset Alzheimer's disease (diagnosis before the age of 65) FTD = Frontotemporal dementia FTLD = Frontotemporal lobar degeneration LBD or LB = Lewy Body disease or dementia MD = Mixed dementia VD = Vascular disease or dementia TBI = Traumatic brain injury CTE = Chronic traumatic encephalopathy NPH = Normal pressure hydrocephalus MCI = Mild Cognitive Impairment YOAD = Younger onset Alzheimer\u2019s disease (another way to say diagnosis before age 65) Stages of Dementia ES = Early stage of Alzheimer's disease (in the beginning of the disease progression) LS = Late Stage of Alzheimer's MS = Middle Stage of Alzheimer's Care Places AL or ALF = Assisted living facility ADC = Adult day care CCC / CCRC / LPC = Continuing care community, continuing care retirement community, or life plan community (a facility which offers independent living, assisted living and nursing home residences) LTC / LTSC = Long-term care / skilled care MC = Memory care NH = Nursing home RCF = Residential care facility (group home, personal care home, adult family home) SNF = Skilled nursing facility/nursing home Medical CNA = Certified nursing assistant Delusion = false ideas that are firmly believed in spite of contradictory proof DNR = Do not resuscitate DON = Director of nursing DVT = Deep vein thrombosis DX = Diagnosis ER = Emergency room G-Tube = Gastrostomy tube Hallucination = false perceptions of objects or events involving the senses; seeing, hearing or tasting things that are not there LPN = Licensed practical nurse LVN = Licensed vocational nurse MMSE = Mini mental state exam OT = Occupational therapy PCP = Primary care physician PEG Tube = percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy tube (feeding tube inserted direct into the abdomen) PT = Physical therapy RN = Registered nurse SLT \u2013 Speech/language therapy TIA = Transient ischemic attack (mini-stroke) UTI = Urinary tract infection Legal APS = Adult protective services CELA = Certified elder law attorney DPOA = Durable power of attorney HIPAA = Law Health Insurance Provider Accountability Act LTCO = Long term care ombudsman LW = Living will NAELA = National Academy of Elder Law Attorneys POA = Power of attorney", "uuid": "4546a1c0-3d1f-484e-8106-512afde3301b"}
{"line_num": "72", "sentence": "Hi everyone ,My name is Kerry.", "uuid": "9449cce8-b527-4080-ab2e-922906843f68"}
{"line_num": "73", "sentence": "I\u2019m living with dementia, and like many of you, I\u2019m navigating a lot of feelings and emotions.", "uuid": "9449cce8-b527-4080-ab2e-922906843f68"}
{"line_num": "74", "sentence": "I\u2019ve reached a point where I\u2019m really craving connection with others who understand this from the inside, not as caregivers, not as observers, but as people living it every day.", "uuid": "9449cce8-b527-4080-ab2e-922906843f68"}
{"line_num": "75", "sentence": "I\u2019ve noticed that many posts here are one\u2011time questions, and while those are helpful, I often find myself wishing for something more ongoing.", "uuid": "9449cce8-b527-4080-ab2e-922906843f68"}
{"line_num": "76", "sentence": "A place where we can return, talk honestly, and build a sense of continuity with people who \u201cget it.\u201d I\u2019m hoping to start a small, steady discussion group just for people living with dementia .", "uuid": "9449cce8-b527-4080-ab2e-922906843f68"}
{"line_num": "77", "sentence": "A space where we don\u2019t have to explain ourselves, apologize for forgetting, or pretend we\u2019re doing better than we are.", "uuid": "9449cce8-b527-4080-ab2e-922906843f68"}
{"line_num": "78", "sentence": "A space where we can simply be real.", "uuid": "9449cce8-b527-4080-ab2e-922906843f68"}
{"line_num": "79", "sentence": "A place where we can: Share the everyday moments\u2014good, bad, confusing, or funny Talk about the fears we usually keep to ourselves Celebrate the small victories Support each other through the tougher days Come back and continue the conversation over time If you\u2019re someone who wants a consistent, understanding place to talk with others walking this same path, I\u2019d love to connect.", "uuid": "9449cce8-b527-4080-ab2e-922906843f68"}
{"line_num": "80", "sentence": "If a few of us are interested, we can shape the group together in whatever way feels right.", "uuid": "9449cce8-b527-4080-ab2e-922906843f68"}
{"line_num": "81", "sentence": "We don\u2019t have to go through this alone.", "uuid": "9449cce8-b527-4080-ab2e-922906843f68"}
{"line_num": "82", "sentence": "I\u2019d really like to build something steady and supportive with others who feel the same.", "uuid": "9449cce8-b527-4080-ab2e-922906843f68"}
{"line_num": "83", "sentence": "With Hope, Kerry", "uuid": "9449cce8-b527-4080-ab2e-922906843f68"}
{"line_num": "84", "sentence": "M, 59.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "85", "sentence": "Wife, sister and kids ganged up on me this summer to get checked out.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "86", "sentence": "They said I kept asking them the same questions and could not correctly recall recent events.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "87", "sentence": "I am a teacher.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "88", "sentence": "I had noticed that I stumbled over some analogies I usually used to go with certain slides.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "89", "sentence": "But, No way I had an impairment, right? They hounded me to get checked.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "90", "sentence": "My neuro said I passed the little card test they gave me and said I'm ok.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "91", "sentence": "But, family insisted I get a second opinion.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "92", "sentence": "Went to the Memory Center at our major hospital.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "93", "sentence": "They did the test and said it wasn't that bad, but they had an experimental blood test that they could use to detect amyloid.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "94", "sentence": "The test came back \"borderline.\" Dr.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "95", "sentence": "said to get a PET scan just in case.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "96", "sentence": "Lit up like a Christmas tree.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "97", "sentence": "Every lobe.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "98", "sentence": "Centiloid score of 144.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "99", "sentence": "My brain is basically rotting from all the plaques.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "100", "sentence": "Tonight, I am nervously waiting for my APOE4 test results to see if it is advisable to go on one of the antibody therapies.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "101", "sentence": "My short term memory is shot.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "102", "sentence": "I am writing everything down like Guy Pearce in Memento (haven't started tattooing anything on me, yet).", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "103", "sentence": "Otherwise, I feel \"normal.\" Just trying to figure out what the new \"normal\" is going to be.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "104", "sentence": "Thinking about how long I might or might not have.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "105", "sentence": "Had long term plans that are likely out the door.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "106", "sentence": "No way I make it to my grandson's HS graduation (he's 2).", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "107", "sentence": "But, then, where do I make it to? And, when do I stop trying to make it? I worked in a retirement home in my high school years.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "108", "sentence": "I have seen where this goes.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "109", "sentence": "I have vivid memories of those days, still.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "110", "sentence": "It was horrible.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "111", "sentence": "No way I am going out like that.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "112", "sentence": "It is either going to be VSED or Switzerland.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "113", "sentence": "I am fortunate that my wife and sister are NP's and support me in this.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "114", "sentence": "Sorry for the dump.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "115", "sentence": "I don't really have any questions, yet.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "116", "sentence": "But, this is the first place I found where there are people in a similar place and I am thankful to all of you for sharing your journey.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "117", "sentence": "Peace to all of you.", "uuid": "8232689b-7584-443d-91ea-f12cc54dd9bc"}
{"line_num": "118", "sentence": "This page contains downloadable PDFs about a wide range of topics related to Alzheimer's and all other dementia.", "uuid": "1ea76233-982a-411a-8539-74f86c3e6863"}
